{"causes":["Omar Khayyám's earlier works in mathematics and astronomy laid the groundwork for his literary pursuits.","Persian literature flourished under the patronage of the Seljuk Empire in the 11th century.","The Mongol Empire's expansion into Persia in the 13th century had a profound impact on the region's culture and literature."],"effects":["The rubáiyát's translations into European languages contributed to the rise of Romanticism in the 19th century.","The quatrains' themes of love and loss have been explored in countless works of literature, influencing the development of modern poetry.","The rubáiyát's blend of mysticism and humor has become a hallmark of Persian literature, inspiring generations of writers and artists."],"relationships":[{"sourceSlug":"seljuk-empire","sourceName":"Seljuk Empire","verb":"INFLUENCES","targetSlug":"rubiyt-of-omar-khayym","targetName":"Rubáiyát of Omar Khayyám","context":"The Seljuk Empire's patronage enabled Omar Khayyám to pursue his literary ambitions."},{"sourceSlug":"mongol-empire","sourceName":"Mongol Empire","verb":"INFLUENCES","targetSlug":"rubiyt-of-omar-khayym","targetName":"Rubáiyát of Omar Khayyám","context":"The Mongol Empire's expansion into Persia led to increased cultural exchange and the spread of Persian literature."},{"sourceSlug":"romanticism","sourceName":"Romanticism","verb":"INFLUENCES","targetSlug":"rubiyt-of-omar-khayym","targetName":"Rubáiyát of Omar Khayyám","context":"The rubáiyát's translations into European languages contributed to the rise of Romanticism in the 19th century."},{"sourceSlug":"islamic-worldview","sourceName":"Islamic worldview","verb":"INFLUENCES","targetSlug":"rubiyt-of-omar-khayym","targetName":"Rubáiyát of Omar Khayyám","context":"The rubáiyát offers a unique window into the medieval Persian worldview, reflecting the cultural and intellectual currents of the time."},{"sourceSlug":"western-literature","sourceName":"Western literature","verb":"INFLUENCES","targetSlug":"rubiyt-of-omar-khayym","targetName":"Rubáiyát of Omar Khayyám","context":"The rubáiyát's influence on Western literature, particularly in the Romantic movement, has been significant."},{"sourceSlug":"medieval-persian-literature","sourceName":"Medieval Persian literature","verb":"TRANSFORMS","targetSlug":"rubiyt-of-omar-khayym","targetName":"Rubáiyát of Omar Khayyám","context":"The rubáiyát represents a pivotal moment in the evolution of Persian literature and its transmission to the West."},{"sourceSlug":"contemporary-literature","sourceName":"Contemporary literature","verb":"INFLUENCES","targetSlug":"rubiyt-of-omar-khayym","targetName":"Rubáiyát of Omar Khayyám","context":"The rubáiyát's themes and style continue to influence contemporary literature and popular culture."},{"sourceSlug":"orientalism","sourceName":"Orientalism","verb":"INFLUENCES","targetSlug":"rubiyt-of-omar-khayym","targetName":"Rubáiyát of Omar Khayyám","context":"The rubáiyát's depiction of Persian culture and society has been criticized for perpetuating Orientalist stereotypes."}],"places":[{"name":"Tus","role":"Birthplace"},{"name":"Samarkand","role":"Residence"},{"name":"Persia","role":"Region"}],"texts":[{"title":"Wikipedia: Rubáiyát of Omar Khayyám","type":"Reference article","slug":"rubáiyát-of-omar-khayyám"}],"externalLinks":["https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q1059358","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rubaiyat_of_Omar_Khayyam"],"tags":["literary work","Historical & Literary Texts","cause-and-effect"],"thumbnailUrl":"","quote":"","legacySummary":"Rubáiyát of Omar Khayyám contributed to the historical record of the Medieval period. Key lasting impacts include: Contributed to cultural heritage and knowledge transmission. Their legacy is studied through the lens of historical causation.","summary":"The Rubáiyát of Omar Khayyám (Persian: رباعیات عمر خیام) is a collection of quatrains (rubāʿī, pl. rubāʿīyāt) attributed to the Persian polymath Omar Khayyám (c. 1048–1131 CE), composed c. 1100 CE and known in the West primarily through Edward FitzGerald's celebrated English adaptation (The Rubáiyát of Omar Khayyám, 1859), which freely rearranged and rendered approximately 75 of the quatrains into English verse. FitzGerald's Rubáiyát is one of the most widely published English poems of the Victorian era and the most influential English-language poem of the 19th century outside England — its themes of hedonistic carpe diem, scepticism about afterlife, and the consolations of wine and companionship in the face of death resonated with Victorian doubters and became a cult text of the fin-de-siècle.

Omar Khayyám was the pre-eminent Persian mathematician and astronomer of his era — he developed the Jalālī calendar (1079 CE, more accurate than the Gregorian), produced systematic solutions to cubic equations, and made fundamental contributions to algebra. The quatrains attributed to him in Persian manuscripts treat themes of wine, love, the brevity of life, the futility of religious dogma, and the uncertainty of existence in a tone that combines Epicurean hedonism with Sufi mystical imagery and a pessimistic metaphysics. The total corpus of quatrains attributed to Khayyám in Persian manuscripts ranges from approximately 250 to over 2,000 (many attributions are spurious or later additions).

FitzGerald's 1859 translation/adaptation — published anonymously, initially ignored, discovered by Dante Gabriel Rossetti and Algernon Swinburne in a penny box at a London bookseller, and subsequently recognised as a masterpiece — is one of the most remarkable cases of translation as creation in literary history: FitzGerald's English poem has a coherence, beauty, and philosophical consistency that arguably exceeds the original quatrains, even as it departs significantly from literal translation.","subjects":["Persian Literature","Medieval Era","Omar Khayyám","Rubāʿī Poetry","FitzGerald Translation","Victorian Literature","Persian Culture","Hedonism"],"frameworks":["STRUCTURAL_ANALYSIS","CAUSE_AND_EFFECT"],"historicalSignificance":{"significanceScore":7,"significanceNarrative":"The Rubáiyát of Omar Khayyám is a significant work of Persian literature that has had a profound impact on the development of Western literature and contemporary literature. Its themes of love, loss, and the transience of life continue to resonate with readers worldwide.","significanceCategory":"regional"},"_editLog":[]}
